body:
When attempting to use workers-ai-provider to create a model with a worker ai hosted embedding model, it generates the error message, `Argument of type '"@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5"' is not assignable to parameter of type 'TextGenerationModels'.ts(2345)`.

Here is the setup I'd like to have, with the main goal of getting the tokens used back:
```
import { embed } from 'ai';
import { createWorkersAI } from "workers-ai-provider";

const workersai = createWorkersAI({ binding: env.AI });

const { embedding, usage } = await embed({
  model: workersai("@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5", {}),
  value: 'sunny day at the beach',
});

console.log(usage.tokens);
```

Yes we can perform the request to get the embedding directly w/o the vercel ai sdk, but I'm not seeing an option to get the token usage back:
```
const { data, shape } = await this.env.AI.run("@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5", {
  text: query,
});
```

Is there a way to either:
- use createWorkersAI with embedding models to get the token usage from the response of vercel ai sdk
- get token usage back directly from the call to the worker ai `run`
